<title>USA: GOLF-SCORES FROM GREENSBORO CLASSIC, WON BY NOBILO.</title>
<headline>GOLF-SCORES FROM GREENSBORO CLASSIC, WON BY NOBILO.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, North Carolina 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>scores after Sunday's final round of the $1.9 million Greater</p>
<p>Greensboro Chrysler Classic played on the 7,062-yard, par-72</p>
<p>Forest Oaks course (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>274 Frank Nobilo (New Zealand) 69 69 69 67, Brad Faxon 67 70</p>
<p>65 72 (Nobilo won playoff with par at first extra hole)</p>
<p>275 Kirk Triplett 67 69 69 70</p>
<p>276 Billy Andrade 72 68 67 69, Robert Damron 66 72 67 71</p>
<p>277 Davis Love 72 69 69 67</p>
<p>278 Mike Standly 68 68 71 71, Tom Kite 67 68 67 76</p>
<p>279 Mark O'Meara 72 67 73 67, Phil Mickelson 71 68 70 70,</p>
<p>Rocco Mediate 72 66 69 72, Ernie Els (South Africa) 69 69 67</p>
<p>74</p>
<p>280 Lennie Clements 70 72 67 71</p>
<p>281 Scott Verplank 72 67 72 70, Fred Funk 69 69 72 71, Jim</p>
<p>Furyk 70 72 68 71, Clarence Rose 70 71 68 72, Paul Stankowski</p>
<p>69 68 69 75</p>
<p>282 Stuart Appleby (Australia) 70 72 71 69, Doug Martin 69 72</p>
<p>71 70, Brent Geiberger 70 70 69 73, John Adams 71 67 70 74,</p>
<p>Glen Day 72 66 69 75, Jerry Kelly 68 69 68 77</p>
<p>Other international players:</p>
<p>283 Naomichi &quot;Joe&quot; Ozaki (Japan) 68 71 68 76</p>
<p>284 Hisayuki Sasaki (Japan) 69 70 69 76</p>
<p>286 Jesper Parnevik (Sweden) 72 70 71 73, Phil Tataurangi</p>
<p>(New Zealand) 71 69 71 75</p>
<p>288 Vijay Singh (Fiji) 69 69 71 79</p>
<p>289 Sandy Lyle (Britain) 66 77 72 74, Steve Elkington</p>
<p>(Australia) 67 71 75 76</p>
<p>291 Hideki Kase (Japan) 73 70 71 77</p>
<p>292 Rafael Alarcon (Mexico) 73 69 73 77</p>
</text>
